ell bodies within submucosal ganglia of the gastrointestinal tract. This cell is located in the submucosa, a layer of connective tissue beneath the intestinal mucosa. This cell plays a role in modulating secretomotor neuron activity and contributes to the regulation of digestive fluid secretion and absorption.\")\n34291:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4047051 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000584 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001902) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q8NFU0)))\n34300:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4047052 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_1000347 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q8NFU0)))\n34310:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4047053 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000235 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000016626)))\n34339:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4047060 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000576 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000004621)))\n34357:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4047101 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000623 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0001025 obo:UBERON_0001281)))\n34583:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052020 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4033040 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003472)))\n34596:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052021 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000909 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003472)))\n34628:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052024 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0005634 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:CL_0008046) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002131 obo:GO_0005927)))\n34640:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052025 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0005634 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:CL_0008046) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002131 obo:GO_0098522)))\n34718:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052032 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000909 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003490)))\n34903:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052051 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4052028 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_O95971) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_P38570) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_P49961) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_P56199) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n34913:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052052 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4052028 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_O95971) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_P38570) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_P49961) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_P56199) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n34923:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052053 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4052028 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030046 obo:PR_P49961) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_O95971) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_P38570) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_P56199) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n34939:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052055 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000814 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_P13591) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)))\n35307:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072015 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0001025 obo:UBERON_0001281))\n35319:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072016 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000011387))\n35329:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072017 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003846))\n35330:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072017 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000011387))\n35372:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072022 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000032148))\n35373:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072022 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000032533))\n35374:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072022 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015004 obo:CLM_1000075))\n35392:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072027 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015004 obo:CLM_1000082))\n35405:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072029 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015004 obo:CLM_1000080))\n35420:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072031 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015004 obo:CLM_1000083))\n35422:# Class: obo:CL_4072032 (VIP GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens))\n35424:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072032 \"VIP interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35429:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26420784\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31210267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33794534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35221922\") terms:description obo:CL_4072032 \"This neuronal type is distinguished by its heterogeneous morphology and electrophysiological characteristics  (Pronneke et al., 2015,2020; Apicella and Marchionni, 2022). Variations in morphology and firing patterns are observed in human VIP interneurons. In a study by Lee et al., 2023, four distinct subtypes of VIP neurons were identified, each exhibiting unique morphologies, soma locations, and electrophysiological properties. These subtypes are defined according to their transcriptomic markers: LBH-VIP and CCD184-VIP, both of which display a bipolar morphology with axons and dendrites extending across cortical layers; and SY16-VIP and ADAMTSL1-VIP, characterized by a dendritic arbor that spreads horizontally within the same layer as the soma (Lee et al., 2023). Disruption or malfunction of VIP interneuron is implicated in neurodevelopmental disorders such as Rett Syndrome and Dravet Syndrome (Goff and Goldberg 2021).\")\n35431:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36384143\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072032 \"VIP neuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35432:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072032 \"VIP type (Homo sapiens)\")\n35433:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33794534\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4072032 \"VIP-IN (Homo sapiens)\")\n35436:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.11165918\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4072032 \"The marker set VIP can identify the Human cell type VIP GABAergic interneuron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.855531344 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35437:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo