{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' PR_COMMENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"Added a new set of myenteric neuron classes to `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` for issue #3584 and committed the change locally.\n\nSummary of changes:\n- Added 14 new CL terms in the `CL_99xxxxx` new-term range for the requested myenteric neuron set.\n- Used existing CL parents already present in `cl-edit.owl`, including `enteric neuron`, `sensory neuron`, `interneuron`, `motor neuron`, `inhibitory motor neuron`, and `dogiel type I neuron`.\n- Added definitions, issue tracker links, `terms:date`, and `terms:creator \"GitHub Copilot\"` for each new class.\n- Added requested synonyms where they were supported by the cited papers.\n- Added conservative logical axioms for the terms that were cleanly compositional:\n  - `intrinsic primary afferent neuron of myenteric plexus`\n  - `interneuron of myenteric plexus`\n  - `cholinergic neuron of myenteric plexus`\n  - `nitrergic neuron of myenteric plexus`\n- Structured the morphology-based subclasses under `dogiel type I neuron` and `dogiel type II neuron`.\n- Added `intestinofugal neuron` with `viscerofugal neuron` as an exact synonym.\n\nModeling decisions:\n- I modeled `secretomotor/vasodilator neuron of myenteric plexus` conservatively. PMID:32888429 supports a transcriptomic PSVN grouping, but PMID:37355216 explicitly notes that direct distinction of secretomotor/vasomotor neurons in the human colonic myenteric plexus was unclear, and PMID:40954253 argues for caution when assigning ENS functional identities from transcriptomics alone. Because of that, I added the term with a minimal hierarchy and an explanatory comment rather than a strong equivalence axiom.\n- I did not add protein-expression axioms for calretinin, VIP, ENK, CART, or related markers, because this environment did not provide a local mapping workflow for the required PR/PRO identifiers and the issue instructions emphasized not guessing ontology IDs. The marker information is still represented in the textual definitions and synonyms where appropriate.\n- I kept the ascending and descending interneuron terms as projection-direction classes under `interneuron of myenteric plexus`, but did not add a directional axon relation because the current file does not already use a stable local pattern for that modeling.\n\nBackground research completed:\n- Read `__issue_context__.json`.\n- Checked existing relevant CL anchor terms directly in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n- Reviewed the cited literature through PubMed/PMC content and metadata:\n  - PMID:34170401\n  - PMID:37355216\n  - PMID:32888429\n  - PMID:38292899\n  - PMID:40954253\n\nValidation and limitations:\n- Performed a manual review of the inserted OWL functional syntax block and the resulting git diff.\n- Could not run `aurelian`, `robot`, or `owltools` in this environment because those commands were not installed.\n\nChecklist:\n- [x] Read the imported issue context.\n- [x] Checked existing parent terms in `cl-edit.owl`.\n- [x] Reviewed the cited publications.\n- [x] Added new terms only in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n- [x] Committed only the edited ontology file.\n- [x] Created `ISSUE_COMMENTS.md`.\n- [x] Created `PR_COMMENTS.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
